  "symbols": [
    {
      "symbol": "Media",
      "status": "modified",
      "kinds": [
        "typed_gap"
      ],
      "fingerprint_before": "db903b1ee676d8c58edd7482288630e6cb2787ace6fe02f936047cec911e8b91",
      "fingerprint_after": "928f43b94f8cc70ee5fff42585eae83b1839897283139f0983515450c8cb40b9",
      "impact": "breaking",
      "reasons": [
        "base classes changed: ['ModelStrict'] -> ['ProvenanceGapMixin']",
        "field 'is_synthetic' type changed: bool -> bool | None",
        "field 'name' type changed: str -> str | None",
        "field 'state' type changed: str -> str | None",
        "validator/serializer changed: ['_stated_or_gapped', 'validate_state']"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "correctness_argument": "Three served datasets have no growth medium to state. SGD's phenotype annotations (pinned dump, SGD_GENES_DIGEST 1cb4ed59...) carry a phenotype and an allele and, on 1,299 of 1,329 annotations, no condition property at all; of the 30 that carry one, 27 read 'nitrogen starvation' and 1 '2% glucose' (nutrient edits to a base medium they do not name), 1 a temperature, and exactly 1 names a medium ('YPD with 2% glucose') without its physical state. SynLethDB 2.0's release carries no condition field: its paper lists what an SL entry stores ('The species, references to PubMed, supporting evidence, cell lines and other relevant information about an SL entry are stored as properties of the edge', paper.md line 49) and r.cell_line is empty on all 14,000 SL and 6,948 SR rows. Before this change the schema could only express such a record by guessing (the old SGD loader stored YEPD solid at 30 C on every record) or by a free-text stand-in Media (#622's 'growth medium not carried by SynLethDB', which joins no shared medium and failed L3 media_membership on 20,938 records, #902). Media now carries ProvenanceGapMixin: name, state and is_synthetic each stay required and are each stated or None beside a ProvenanceGap naming that field, its reason (not_carried_by_curation) and the pinned artifact it was looked for in, with a note quoting the source's silence. This is strictly more correct than either alternative: a record states exactly what its source states and types exactly what it does not, a partly stated medium gaps only what is missing (SGD's 'YPD with 2% glucose' keeps its name on the YPD base and gaps only state), and Environment.media stays a required Media. It accepts no record the old contract would have refused silently: a None label without a gap naming that field is refused (_stated_or_gapped), and a gap beside a value is refused (the mixin). It changes no stated medium's meaning: every existing Media states all three labels, so it validates unchanged and media_identity, which projects gaps only when a medium carries one, gives every stated medium the id it had (the Ohya MEDIA_ID and ENVIRONMENT_ID pins hold). Measured on the rebuilt dev stores (slurm 4184, verified by the committed kg4_pre_build_verification_sweep.py under slurm 4194): gene_essentiality_sgd 1,287 records, syn_leth_db_yeast 13,996, syn_rescue_db_yeast 6,942, and L3 media_membership passes on all three (1,286 + 13,996 + 6,942 records on a typed medium gap, 1 SGD record derived from YPD). The change is breaking for every served closure, because every Media dump now carries an empty provenance_gaps and every experiment id moves; that is accepted by the owner and lands with the KG 4.0 full rebuild.",
  "measurement_type_decision": false,
  "source_quotes": [],
  "alternatives_rejected": [
    {
      "alternative": "Make Environment.media optional (Media | None, None only beside a ProvenanceGap(field='media')), this PR's first draft",
      "why_rejected": "It loosens a required field to fit a thin source (policy Rule 5). The owner reversed it on 2026-10-11: \"i don't think env / media should be optional... if there are some cell growth under some condition i think we need it ... if we are blocked by the compendia... then we shouldn't use that compendia.\""
    },
    {
      "alternative": "Remove the three dataset classes and keep SGD and SynLethDB as provenance records with no loader, this PR's second draft",
      "why_rejected": "It throws away 22,277 served records to protect one field (policy Rule 4). The owner reversed it on 2026-10-12: \"we are fine with irreversible updates to schema, as long as you are convinced it is correct ... why would you get rid of old classes?\""
    },
    {
      "alternative": "Keep a stand-in Media with a placeholder name and state (the #622 'growth medium not carried by SynLethDB' object) or the old guessed YEPD solid at 30 C",
      "why_rejected": "A placeholder reads as a medium somebody stated and joins no shared medium (L3 media_membership failed on 13,996 SL and 6,942 SR records, #902 and #903); a guessed YEPD states a medium no source states (#901). Neither is a typed absence."
    }
  ],
